sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, ADR 0260 build step 4 (docs/reference/development-containers.md#the-seed-on-each-ci-node): each CI Node that hosts proof copies keeps its own seed of the proof Project's default. One run per seed of the default pins the seed once on the default's Node and sends it to every CI Node whose seed is behind; each target may fail alone. Decided by the owner (2026-11-16): the send is incremental. The stream passes the Swamp worker, which is remote from the CI Nodes and short of CPU, and a full seed pair is large; so each CI Node keeps its last seed as the base of the next one, and a full send happens only when a Node has no common seed. Rejected: one seed that every copy fetches over the network at its start (ADR 0260), a seed Instance per CI Node that refreshes its own fleet, and an Incus copy between Nodes, which needs Incus API trust between them.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · after the proof default records a seed, or a CI Node's ci-runner add or converge passes
  %% kind: instance.seed_copy
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Default Node<br/>holds the default
  participant C as CI Node<br/>each target
  Note over GW: Admit the seed copy<br/>CI Nodes behind the seed
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - the proof default records a new seed: the refresh after a release, or an `instance:deploy` of the default
  %%> - a `ci-runner` add or converge of a CI Node that hosts proof copies passes
  %%> - a seed copy ends: for the Nodes it did not try at the default's current seed
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the proof Project's default is active and has a seed; a seed is its commit and the time the default took it
  %%> - targets: every CI Node that hosts proof copies whose recorded seed is not that seed (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#proof-copies-on-a-ci-node); with none, nothing is admitted
  %%> - one copy at a time: an open copy holds the default's seed-copy lock, `operation.target_busy`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent: the default's Node and seed pair, the recorded holder of every CI Node that hosts proof copies, and per target the new holder `proof-seed-OPERATION`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>instance-seed-copy
  SW->>N: Pin the seed<br/>ZFS clones of the seed pair
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - copies the container snapshot `seed-COMMIT` and the volume snapshot of the same name into the stopped pair `seed-copy-OPERATION`, as ZFS clones
  %%> - takes the default's seed lock on the Node, the one the seed step holds during a retake, so it never reads a pair that a retake is replacing
  %%> - marks both snapshots of the seed pair with the ZFS bookmark `proof-seed-OPERATION`: the default's half of the next base; a bookmark holds no data and never stops a retake from deleting an old seed
  %%> - first deletes a pinned pair that an earlier run left
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a later retake of the default cannot change what the copy reads; one pin serves every target, so it takes one ID range on the default's Node
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - no free ID range, or the seed is gone: `instance.seed_copy_failed`; no target is tried
  loop each CI Node, side by side
    SW->>C: Choose the base<br/>recorded holder · bookmark
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - first deletes each holder on the Node that is neither recorded nor this run's, so an old holder goes only after the Gateway checked and recorded the new one
    %%> - the base is the recorded holder `proof-seed-X` when its snapshot `seed-COMMIT` and its volume's snapshot are on the Node and the bookmark `proof-seed-X` is on both datasets of the default's Node
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the last seed the Node received is the base of the next one; the bookmark is the same snapshot on the default's side, so `zfs send -i` can start from it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - with no base (the Node's first seed, or a failure lost it): this target gets a full send; the other targets are not changed
    SW->>C: Send the seed<br/>zfs send -i · SSH stream
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - with a base: makes the new holder `proof-seed-OPERATION` and its volume `proof-seed-OPERATION-inner` in `orbit-instances-nested` as clones of the base, beside the recorded holder; sends the change from the bookmark to the seed, for the container and for its volume (`zfs send -i`)
    %%> - without a base: sends the full seed pair into the new holder and its volume
    %%> - streams from `zfs send` on the default's Node through the worker's two SSH connections straight into `zfs receive` on the CI Node; nothing stays on the worker or in a file
    %%> - the received snapshot is the holder's snapshot `seed-COMMIT`; Incus takes no new one, so the snapshot keeps the identity the next change needs
    %%> - the holder never starts
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the worker is remote from the CI Nodes and short of CPU, and a full seed pair is large; a release changes a small part of it
    %%> - the worker already reaches both Nodes over SSH; no Node trusts another
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - no free ID range for the new holder: the detail says `No free ID range for the new seed`
    SW->>C: Check the holder<br/>start guard rules
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the holder's config and devices match the default's, as the start guard checks them; the volume has exactly the inner volume's keys
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - this target fails with `instance.seed_copy_failed` and deletes what it made on its Node; its recorded holder stays, and it is the base of the next copy; the other targets go on
  end
  SW->>N: Unpin the seed<br/>condition: always
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes the pinned pair, also after a failed target or a failed pin
  %%> - deletes each bookmark `proof-seed-*` that is neither this run's nor named by a CI Node's recorded holder
  SW-->>GW: Run ended<br/>result per target
  %%> How the Gateway learns it:
  %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
  Note over GW: Record each new seed
  %%> Result:
  %%> - each Node whose target passed records the new holder, its commit and its time as its seed; it offers proof places again
  %%> - a proof copy on that Node clones the recorded holder with the clone step of every copy
  opt a target or the pin failed
    Note over GW: Keep the old seed<br/>Activity per failed Node
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the failed Node keeps its recorded holder and offers no proof places until a copy passes; copies made earlier keep running
    %%> - the Activity row `instance.seed_copy_failed` names the Node, the Operation and the detail
    %%> - the release and the default are unchanged; the next trigger copies again, and a rerun is safe
  end
  opt the default's seed moved
    Note over GW: Admit the next copy<br/>Nodes not tried at it
    %%> When:
    %%> - the default took a newer seed while the copy ran, or a Node became a target while the copy held the lock
  end
